/* Initialise the CoreFn FileSwitch-handler state.
 *
 * Marks every FileTbl slot as free and resets the round-robin allocator cursor.  Called from LM_init_phase_2, which runs
 * after LM_Declare has made the filing system live, and again whenever a service call re-runs that phase.
 *
 * Returns: always true; the bool is kept for symmetry with other *_Init entry points.
 */
extern bool FS_Init(void);

/* Drop every directory snapshot, so the next call of a pass over any directory reads it from the cache or the server.
 *
 * A pass over a directory is answered from a copy of its listing taken at the pass's first call.  Anything that changes how its names
 * are shown, or what a mount name stands for, must call this, as must anything in CoreFn that changes an object on the server.
 */
extern void CoreFn_ForgetSnapshots(void);
